<ArticleLayout
  title="Garage Hive Alternatives (2026) | GarageCloud"
  description="Looking for a Garage Hive alternative? A straight comparison of TechMan, Dragon2000, Motasoft and GarageCloud on pricing and who each is built for."
  eyebrow="Comparison"
  breadcrumbLabel="Garage Hive alternatives"
  heading="Garage Hive alternatives"
  lede="Garage Hive runs on Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central, which adds a platform licence on top of its own fee. Here's what else is out there, and what each actually costs."
>
  <p>
    <strong>The most common reason workshops look for a Garage Hive alternative is the combined cost.</strong>
    Garage Hive's own licence starts from £145/month, but it's an add-on to Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central
    — which carries its own per-user Microsoft licence on top, commonly pushing the real cost past £250/month for a
    small team (see <a href="https://garagehive.co.uk/pricing/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Garage
    Hive's pricing page</a>). If that combined cost doesn't make sense for the size of the workshop, these are the
    main alternatives worth knowing about.
  </p>

  <h2>TechMan</h2>
  <p>
    The UK's most established garage system, with 14,500+ active users and 15+ years in the market. Three tiers —
    £189, £315 and £415/month — tied to a 3-year contract. Strong fit for a workshop that wants a mature, deeply
    integrated system (Autodata, multi-location support) and is comfortable committing to a long-term contract.
    See our <a href="/vs/techman">full GarageCloud vs TechMan comparison</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Dragon2000 (DragonDMS)</h2>
  <p>
    £99.95 per user, per month. Over 30 years in the market, but aimed primarily at car dealerships — it includes
    stock and finance administration alongside workshop tools. A strong option for a dealership; less relevant for
    an independent garage that doesn't need dealership-specific features.
    See our <a href="/vs/dragon2000">full GarageCloud vs Dragon2000 comparison</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Motasoft (Virtual Garage Manager)</h2>
  <p>
    Base pricing from £50–£120/month, with VRM lookups, SMS and MOT data refresh billed as separate credits on top.
    Close to two decades in the market and a direct GroupTyre integration. A strong low-entry-price option if the
    credit-based add-ons work for how the workshop operates.
    See our <a href="/vs/motasoft">full GarageCloud vs Motasoft comparison</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>GarageCloud</h2>
  <p>
    A standalone system — no separate platform licence required — priced per workshop rather than per user, from
    £50/month excluding VAT with no long-term contract. GarageCloud is pre-launch, onboarding workshops from a
    waiting list, so it doesn't yet have the track record of the systems above. It's built for workshops that want
    to start on a flat monthly fee without committing to a multi-year contract or a Business Central licence. See <a href="/garage-management-software">what garage management software covers</a> and <a href="/pricing">GarageCloud pricing</a>, or <a href="/vs/garage-hive">the full GarageCloud vs Garage Hive comparison</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>How to choose</h2>
  <p>
    The honest answer depends on what the workshop already has. Deep into Microsoft 365 already: Garage Hive. A
    dealership needing stock and finance tools: Dragon2000. Want the most established option and can commit to a
    3-year term: TechMan. Want the lowest possible entry price and don't mind credit-based add-ons: Motasoft. Want a
    flat monthly fee, no long contract, and don't need dealership tooling: GarageCloud.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
